            <ArticleTitle>Lyme disease: an unusual case of peripheral nerve palsy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>713-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1302/0301-620X.92B5.23345</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lyme disease is a vector-borne multisystem inflammatory disease caused by the spirochete Borrelia burgdorferi sensu lato. This disease is frequently seen in North America and to a lesser degree in Europe. However, its presence in England is uncommon and we present a case in which the patient developed a palsy of the common peroneal nerve.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
